ction tests (8080 reachable, an unrelated port refused), and confirmed to survive a full node reboot with identical rules and active/enabled state afterward. The mandatory single-node restart evidence protocol was also completed with a clean pre/post boot-identity transition corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots.","limitations":["Only one unrelated port (9999) was tested for rejection; broader port-scan evidence was not captured, though the nftables ruleset dump independently confirms no other accept rules exist.","Only a single reboot cycle was captured for the restart-persistence check; no additional stress (e.g., repeated reboots or service restarts) was observed.","IPv6 reachability of SSH/8080 was inferred from nftables rule presence but not live-tested (only IPv4 curl/nc tests were run)."]},"ttft_ms":19211,"type":"result","duration_ms":59596,"uuid":"64c26fb2-bf58-4f1d-912d-7d4f55159e11","ttft_stream_ms":2001,"time_to_request_ms":48,"queued_turn_count":0}
